        "original_id": "9694e7e6-f7fd-581f-9fee-0e5697e0b42a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 67th Venice International Film Festival, Antofagasta Film Festival, Havana Film Festival, Guadalajara International Film Festival\n- Places: Venice, Italy\n- Films: Black Swan, Post Mortem\n- People: Darren Aronofsky, Natalie Portman, Vincent Cassel, Mila Kunis, Barbara Hershey, Winona Ryder, Scott Franklin\n- Awards: Academy Awards, Independent Spirit Award for Best Picture\n\nFacts:\n- The 67th Venice International Film Festival was held in Venice, Italy, from 1 to 11 September 2010.\n- The opening film of the 67th Venice International Film Festival was Darren Aronofsky's Black Swan.\n- Black Swan stars Natalie Portman, Vincent Cassel, Mila Kunis, Barbara Hershey, and Winona Ryder.\n- Post Mortem competed in the 67th Venice International Film Festival, the Antofagasta Film Festival, the Havana Film Festival, and the Guadalajara International Film Festival.\n- Scott Franklin was nominated for an Academy Award for his work on Black Swan.\n- Scott Franklin received the Independent Spirit Award for Best Picture twice.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
